<title>JAPAN: Kyushu refinery, nuclear plants unaffected by rain.</title>
<headline>Kyushu refinery, nuclear plants unaffected by rain.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>An oil refinery and two nuclear power plants on Japan's southern island of Kyushu are operating normally despite heavy rains that triggered a landslide and killed at least 13 people, company officials said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;There has been no damage to our facilities and no changes in plant operations,&quot; said a spokesman for Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc.</p>
<p>One of the two nuclear power plants run by Kyushu Electric is located in Sendai, Kagoshima prefecture, just 30 kilometres (19 miles) south of the scene of the landslide.</p>
<p>Kyushu Oil Co Ltd said its 136,000 barrel-per-day plant in Oita prefecture was up and running normally.</p>
<p>The Oita plant is the sole oil refinery on the island.</p>
</text>
